    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0139" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/1037: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hamilton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-02T19:00:00+03:00">May 2, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 3—1:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1547. Please inform the Secretary of the Treasury, in further reference to your
                    1052, April 27, 8 [<hi rendition="#italic">7</hi>] p.m. that Vyshinski<anchor
                        n="35" xml:id="d95-f1"/> told me <pb facs="0140" n="130" xml:id="pg130"/>
                    this evening that the Soviet Government’s reply to the question raised by Mr.
                    Morgenthau was that the Soviet Government is prepared to accept an invitation to
                    send a delegation to a monetary conference at the end of May. Vyshinski stated
                    further that while the Commissar for Finance would like to head the Soviet
                    delegation, he could not do so since he was too busy here. Vyshinski continued
                    that the Soviet delegation would be selected subsequently.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d95-f1" n="35" xml:id="d95-f1-content">
                <p>Andrey Yanuaryevich Vyshinski, Soviet Assistant People’s Commissar for Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
